# macOS signing + notarization credentials — copy to .env.signing (GITIGNORED) and fill in
# after enrolling in the Apple Developer Program. scripts/release.sh sources .env.signing
# automatically; when it's absent, builds stay unsigned exactly as before.
#
# 1) Certificate: Xcode → Settings → Accounts → Manage Certificates → + → Developer ID Application
#    Then find the exact identity string:  security find-identity -v -p codesigning
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: YOUR NAME (TEAMID)"

# 2) Notarization — App Store Connect API key (recommended; no 2FA at build time):
#    appstoreconnect.apple.com → Users and Access → Integrations → App Store Connect API → +
#    Role: Developer. Download the .p8 ONCE and store it OUTSIDE the repo.
APPLE_API_ISSUER="00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
APPLE_API_KEY="ABC123DEFG"
APPLE_API_KEY_PATH="$HOME/.appstoreconnect/AuthKey_ABC123DEFG.p8"

# (Alternative to the API key — Apple ID flow; leave the three above unset if using this)
# APPLE_ID="you@example.com"
# APPLE_PASSWORD="app-specific-password"   # appleid.apple.com → App-Specific Passwords
# APPLE_TEAM_ID="TEAMID"
